var e={id:`iceland`,name:`Iceland`,localName:`Ísland`,flag:`🇮🇸`,currency:`ISK`,language:`Icelandic, English widely spoken`,greeting:{text:`Velkomin`,meaning:`Welcome`},bestMonths:[2,3,6,7,8,9],tips:[`The weather turns fast: pack waterproof layers year-round, and check vedur.is for the forecast and safetravel.is for alerts before every drive.`,`Check umferdin.is for road conditions. F-roads into the highlands open only around late June to September and need a 4x4 by law; rental insurance rarely covers river crossings.`,`Never stop on the road for photos, give way at single-lane bridges, and respect the speed limits; cameras are common and fines are steep.`,`Iceland is expensive: cards work almost everywhere, tap water is excellent, and supermarkets such as Bónus and Krónan keep picnic lunches cheap.`,`Northern lights season runs roughly September to April. Watch the aurora and cloud forecasts on vedur.is and head away from town lights on clear nights.`,`At black-sand beaches like Reynisfjara, sneaker waves kill visitors every few years: stay well back from the water and never turn your back on the sea.`],cities:[{id:`reykjavik`,name:`Reykjavík`,lat:64.14583,lng:-21.9425,timezone:`Atlantic/Reykjavik`,tagline:`Colourful capital of hot pools, design and Golden Circle days`,description:`The world's northernmost capital is a small, walkable city of corrugated-iron houses, bold modern architecture, geothermal pools and a lively food and bar scene. It is also the base for Iceland's classic day trips: the Golden Circle's rift valley, geysers and waterfalls, the Blue Lagoon on the Reykjanes lava fields, and the Snæfellsnes peninsula.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`hallgrimskirkja`,name:`Hallgrímskirkja`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`,`tower`],area:`Skólavörðuholt`,lat:64.1417,lng:-21.9266,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:5,description:`Reykjavík's soaring concrete church, its stepped facade inspired by basalt columns, with a lift up the 74-metre tower for the best view over the city's coloured roofs.`,tip:`Entry to the church is free; buy a tower ticket inside. The tower closes during services, and the organ is worth hearing if a recital is on.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Hallgrímskirkja`},{id:`harpa`,name:`Harpa Concert Hall`,localName:`Harpa`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`architecture`,`concerts`,`waterfront`,`glass`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Old Harbour`,lat:64.15028,lng:-21.9325,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The harbourside concert hall whose glass facade by Ólafur Elíasson glitters like basalt crystals, home to the Iceland Symphony Orchestra and the opera.`,tip:`The foyer is free to wander; come at dusk when the facade lights up, or catch a concert or a comedy show in English.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Harpa (concert hall)`},{id:`sun-voyager`,name:`Sun Voyager`,localName:`Sólfar`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`sculpture`,`waterfront`,`sunset`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Sæbraut`,lat:64.1476,lng:-21.92231,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A stainless-steel sculpture of a dreamlike Viking-style ship on the seafront, looking across the bay to Mount Esja.`,tip:`Best at sunset; walk the seafront path from here to Harpa.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`The Sun Voyager`},{id:`national-museum-of-iceland`,name:`National Museum of Iceland`,localName:`Þjóðminjasafn Íslands`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`vikings`,`medieval`,`rainy-day`],area:`Melar`,lat:64.14194,lng:-21.94806,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`The country's story from the first settlers to today, with Viking-age swords and silver, the carved Valþjófsstaður church door and rooms of everyday life.`,tip:`The permanent exhibition is the highlight; leave at least 90 minutes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of Iceland`},{id:`perlan`,name:`Perlan`,category:`museum`,tags:[`nature-exhibition`,`ice-cave`,`planetarium`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Öskjuhlíð`,lat:64.1292,lng:-21.9189,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A glass dome on top of hot-water tanks, housing an indoor ice cave, a glacier and volcano exhibition, a northern lights planetarium show and a 360-degree viewing deck.`,tip:`The planetarium aurora show is a good stand-in on cloudy nights; walk down through the Öskjuhlíð woods to Nauthólsvík.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Perlan`},{id:`hafnarhus`,name:`Reykjavík Art Museum Hafnarhús`,localName:`Hafnarhús`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`erro`,`rainy-day`],area:`Old Harbour`,lat:64.14965,lng:-21.93975,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`The contemporary branch of the city art museum in a former harbour warehouse, with rotating shows and a large collection of the pop artist Erró.`,tip:`One ticket covers all three Reykjavík Art Museum sites on the same day, including Kjarvalsstaðir and Ásmundarsafn.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Reykjavik Art Museum`},{id:`kjarvalsstadir`,name:`Kjarvalsstaðir`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`painting`,`modernism`,`park`,`rainy-day`],area:`Klambratún`,lat:64.13787,lng:-21.91395,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A 1970s modernist gallery in Klambratún park devoted to Jóhannes Kjarval, whose mossy, mystical lava landscapes shaped how Icelanders see their land.`,tip:`Uses the same day ticket as Hafnarhús; the café looks out over the park.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Reykjavik Art Museum`},{id:`tjornin`,name:`Tjörnin`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lake`,`birds`,`walking`,`park`,`free`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14444,lng:-21.9425,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The pond in the middle of the city, ringed by pastel houses and churches and full of swans, ducks and geese; in winter part of it freezes for skating.`,tip:`Loop round it via the Hljómskálagarður park and pop into City Hall on the north shore.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tjörnin`},{id:`reykjavik-city-hall`,name:`Reykjavík City Hall`,localName:`Ráðhús Reykjavíkur`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`architecture`,`relief-map`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14583,lng:-21.94222,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A concrete-and-glass city hall that seems to float on the pond, with a big 3D relief map of Iceland in the public hall.`,tip:`Free to enter on weekdays; the relief map is handy for planning a road trip.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Reykjavík Town Hall`},{id:`althingishusid`,name:`Parliament House and Austurvöllur`,localName:`Alþingishúsið`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`parliament`,`square`,`history`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14667,lng:-21.94028,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The modest 1881 basalt home of the Alþingi, one of the world's oldest parliaments, facing the grassy Austurvöllur square where locals sun themselves in summer.`,tip:`The square fills with people on sunny days and is the site of national celebrations on 17 June.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Alþingishúsið`},{id:`laugavegur`,name:`Laugavegur`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`main-street`,`design`,`wool`,`cafes`,`walking`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14446,lng:-21.92343,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Reykjavík's main shopping street, running from the old centre to Hlemmur past design stores, wool shops, record stores, cafés and bars.`,tip:`Shops close around 18:00 but bars stay open late; tax-free shopping refunds apply over a minimum spend.`,indoor:!1},{id:`skolavordustigur`,name:`Skólavörðustígur Rainbow Street`,localName:`Skólavörðustígur`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`rainbow`,`galleries`,`design`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14411,lng:-21.9299,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The street climbing from Laugavegur to Hallgrímskirkja, with a rainbow painted on the paving and small galleries, jewellers and craft shops along the way.`,tip:`Frame your photo with the church at the top of the hill.`,indoor:!1},{id:`old-harbour`,name:`Old Harbour`,localName:`Gamla höfnin`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`harbour`,`boats`,`seafood`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Old Harbour`,lat:64.1508,lng:-21.9425,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The working harbour west of Harpa, with whale-watching boats, fishing trawlers and old harbour sheds turned into seafood restaurants, shops and museums.`,tip:`Walk west along Grandagarður to the Grandi district for more museums, galleries and a food hall.`,indoor:!1},{id:`whale-watching`,name:`Reykjavík Whale Watching`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`whales`,`boat-tour`,`puffins`,`wildlife`],area:`Old Harbour`,lat:64.15172,lng:-21.9432,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:115,rating:4,description:`Boats leave the Old Harbour for Faxaflói Bay to look for minke and humpback whales, white-beaked dolphins and, from May to August, puffins on nearby islets.`,tip:`Summer is best; dress warmly even in July and choose an operator that offers a free re-trip if you see no whales.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saga-museum`,name:`Saga Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`vikings`,`history`,`wax-figures`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Grandi`,lat:64.15256,lng:-21.95128,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:3,description:`Lifelike silicone figures act out key moments of Icelandic history, from the first settlers and saga heroes to the Black Death and the Reformation.`,tip:`The audio guide brings it to life; there is a dressing-up corner with Viking costumes at the end.`,indoor:!0},{id:`whales-of-iceland`,name:`Whales of Iceland`,category:`family`,tags:[`whales`,`life-size-models`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Grandi`,lat:64.1556,lng:-21.9488,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:37,rating:4,description:`A big hall of life-size models of the 23 whale species seen around Iceland, including a full-size blue whale, under a dim, underwater-blue light.`,tip:`A good add-on to a whale-watching trip, or a substitute when boats are cancelled by weather.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Whales of Iceland`},{id:`flyover-iceland`,name:`FlyOver Iceland`,category:`family`,tags:[`flight-ride`,`film`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Grandi`,lat:64.15658,lng:-21.94879,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:49,rating:4,description:`A flight-ride theatre where your seat swings in front of a giant dome screen for a soaring tour over Iceland's glaciers, volcanoes and fjords, with wind and mist effects.`,tip:`Book a slot online; the pre-show rooms add folklore before the ride.`,indoor:!0},{id:`aurora-reykjavik`,name:`Aurora Reykjavík`,category:`museum`,tags:[`northern-lights`,`exhibition`,`photography`,`rainy-day`],area:`Grandi`,lat:64.15638,lng:-21.94469,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`A small northern lights centre explaining the science and myths of the aurora, with time-lapse films and tips on how to photograph it.`,tip:`Go early in your trip so you know how to set up your camera before an aurora night.`,indoor:!0},{id:`lava-show`,name:`Lava Show Reykjavík`,category:`family`,tags:[`lava`,`show`,`volcano`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Grandi`,lat:64.15699,lng:-21.94297,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:57,rating:4,description:`Real lava, melted at over 1,100 °C, flows into a small theatre a few metres from your seat while guides explain Icelandic eruptions.`,tip:`Book ahead; evening shows suit days spent out of town.`,indoor:!0},{id:`settlement-exhibition`,name:`Settlement Exhibition`,localName:`Landnámssýningin`,category:`museum`,tags:[`vikings`,`archaeology`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14751,lng:-21.94281,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`The excavated ruins of a 10th-century longhouse, found in situ under a downtown street, with screens and finds recreating the earliest days of Reykjavík.`,tip:`Part of the City Museum: the ticket also covers Árbæjarsafn and the Maritime Museum.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Settlement Exhibition`},{id:`phallological-museum`,name:`Icelandic Phallological Museum`,localName:`Hið íslenska reðasafn`,category:`museum`,tags:[`quirky`,`unusual`,`humour`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14862,lng:-21.93583,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:29,rating:3,description:`The world's only museum of penises, with specimens from almost every Icelandic mammal plus folklore exhibits, presented with a scientific straight face and lots of humour.`,tip:`It is near Hafnartorg by the harbour and has a café-bar serving phallic waffles.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Icelandic Phallological Museum`},{id:`national-gallery`,name:`National Gallery of Iceland`,localName:`Listasafn Íslands`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`painting`,`icelandic-art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.14411,lng:-21.93925,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`Iceland's main collection of 19th and 20th century art, in a white former ice house by the pond, with shows from Kjarval and Þórarinn Þorláksson to contemporary artists.`,tip:`The ticket also covers the Ásgrímur Jónsson studio home nearby.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Gallery of Iceland`},{id:`arbaejarsafn`,name:`Árbær Open Air Museum`,localName:`Árbæjarsafn`,category:`culture`,tags:[`open-air-museum`,`turf-houses`,`history`,`kids`],area:`Árbær`,lat:64.11848,lng:-21.81838,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A village of more than 20 relocated old houses, from turf farmhouses to a church and town houses, showing how Icelanders lived before modern Reykjavík.`,tip:`In summer, staff in period dress run demonstrations; in winter it opens only for guided tours.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Árbæjarsafn`},{id:`hofdi`,name:`Höfði House`,localName:`Höfði`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`history`,`cold-war`,`waterfront`,`free`],area:`Borgartún`,lat:64.14639,lng:-21.90667,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The white wooden house on the seafront where Reagan and Gorbachev met in 1986, the summit that helped thaw the Cold War.`,tip:`The inside is not open to visitors; see it from outside on a seafront walk from Sun Voyager.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Höfði`},{id:`grotta`,name:`Grótta Lighthouse`,localName:`Grótta`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lighthouse`,`northern-lights`,`sunset`,`birds`,`foot-bath`,`free`],area:`Seltjarnarnes`,lat:64.1644,lng:-22.022,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A tidal island with a lighthouse at the western tip of the Seltjarnarnes peninsula, a favourite for sunsets and one of the darkest places in town to watch the northern lights.`,tip:`Soak your feet in the small geothermal foot bath by the shore; the island is cut off at high tide and closed in bird nesting season (May to July).`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Grótta`},{id:`videy`,name:`Viðey Island`,localName:`Viðey`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`ferry`,`art`,`imagine-peace-tower`,`walking`],area:`Kollafjörður`,lat:64.16667,lng:-21.86667,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:21,rating:3,description:`A peaceful island a short ferry ride from the city, with walking trails, Richard Serra's Milestones sculptures, an 18th-century church and Yoko Ono's Imagine Peace Tower.`,tip:`The ferry runs often in summer and only at weekends in winter; the Peace Tower beam shines from 9 October to 8 December.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Viðey`},{id:`sky-lagoon`,name:`Sky Lagoon`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`lagoon`,`spa`,`ocean-view`,`sunset`,`northern-lights`],area:`Kársnes (Kópavogur)`,lat:64.11649,lng:-21.94887,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`An oceanside geothermal lagoon with an infinity edge facing the North Atlantic, turf-walled buildings and a seven-step sauna and cold-plunge ritual.`,tip:`Book a sunset slot; it is only 15 minutes from downtown, so it fits an evening after a day trip.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sky Lagoon`},{id:`laugardalslaug`,name:`Laugardalslaug`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`swimming`,`hot-tub`,`local-life`,`kids`],area:`Laugardalur`,lat:64.14583,lng:-21.88028,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`The city's biggest geothermal pool complex, with an Olympic-size outdoor pool, a row of hot tubs, a seawater tub, a steam bath and slides, open late every day.`,tip:`The local alternative to the lagoons at a tenth of the price. Shower without a swimsuit before entering, as everyone does.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Laugardalslaug`},{id:`sundholl`,name:`Sundhöllin`,localName:`Sundhöll Reykjavíkur`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`art-deco`,`hot-tub`,`local-life`,`rainy-day`],area:`Miðborg`,lat:64.1417,lng:-21.9203,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`The city's oldest public baths, a 1937 Guðjón Samúelsson building with an elegant indoor pool, plus newer outdoor hot tubs and a lap pool.`,tip:`A five-minute walk from Hallgrímskirkja; the indoor pool is perfect on stormy days.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sundhöll Reykjavíkur`},{id:`nautholsvik`,name:`Nauthólsvík Geothermal Beach`,localName:`Nauthólsvík`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`geothermal`,`hot-tub`,`sea-swimming`],area:`Öskjuhlíð`,lat:64.1212,lng:-21.9285,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`A golden-sand beach in a sheltered cove where geothermal water warms a lagoon and hot tubs, so locals can swim in the sea year-round.`,tip:`Free in summer, with a small fee in winter; changing rooms and showers are on site.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Nauthólsvík`},{id:`family-park-and-zoo`,name:`Reykjavík Family Park and Zoo`,localName:`Fjölskyldu- og húsdýragarðurinn`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`farm-animals`,`kids`,`playground`,`seals`],area:`Laugardalur`,lat:64.13864,lng:-21.8715,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:3,description:`A small zoo of Icelandic animals, from seals, reindeer and Arctic foxes to horses, sheep and goats, with rides and playgrounds next door.`,tip:`Pair it with the free Botanic Garden next door and its pretty café.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kolaportid`,name:`Kolaportið Flea Market`,localName:`Kolaportið`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`flea-market`,`weekend`,`fermented-shark`,`local-life`,`rainy-day`,`free`],area:`Old Harbour`,lat:64.14889,lng:-21.93861,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An indoor weekend flea market in an old harbour customs building, selling second-hand wool sweaters, records, books and Icelandic food oddities.`,tip:`Open Saturdays and Sundays only; the food corner is where to try fermented shark and dried fish.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Kolaportið`},{id:`downtown-bars`,name:`Downtown Bars and Live Music`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`happy-hour`,`live-music`,`weekend`],area:`Laugavegur and Bankastræti`,lat:64.1465,lng:-21.932,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`Reykjavík's compact bar scene runs along Laugavegur, Bankastræti and Austurstræti, from cosy pubs and craft-beer bars to clubs that fill after midnight at weekends.`,tip:`Drinks are pricey, so use the early-evening happy hours; Friday and Saturday nights are busiest.`,indoor:!0},{id:`golden-circle`,name:`Golden Circle Day Trip`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`geysers`,`waterfall`,`national-park`,`rift-valley`,`iconic`],area:`South Iceland`,lat:64.3137,lng:-20.2995,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:5,description:`The classic loop from Reykjavík: the rift valley of Þingvellir National Park, the erupting Strokkur geyser at Geysir, and the two-tiered Gullfoss waterfall, often with the Kerið crater lake.`,tip:`Self-drive or join a tour; start early to beat the coaches, and add a soak at a lagoon such as Laugarvatn Fontana or the Secret Lagoon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Golden Circle (Iceland)`},{id:`blue-lagoon`,name:`Blue Lagoon`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`lagoon`,`spa`,`silica-mud`,`iconic`],area:`Reykjanes Peninsula`,lat:63.88,lng:-22.44806,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:130,rating:5,description:`Iceland's most famous spa, a milky-blue geothermal lagoon in a black lava field, with silica mud masks and a swim-up bar, 45 minutes from the city.`,tip:`Pre-booking is mandatory. It suits arrival or departure day as it is near the airport; check safetravel.is as nearby eruptions have closed it at times.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Blue Lagoon (geothermal spa)`},{id:`snaefellsnes`,name:`Snæfellsnes Peninsula Day Trip`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`kirkjufell`,`glacier`,`beaches`,`iconic`,`coastal`],area:`West Iceland`,lat:64.94104,lng:-23.30569,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`Iceland in miniature: the arrow-shaped Kirkjufell mountain, the Snæfellsjökull glacier volcano, the black church at Búðir, sea cliffs at Arnarstapi and the pebbles of Djúpalónssandur.`,tip:`A very long day from Reykjavík, about 2.5 hours each way; if you can, stay a night on the peninsula.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Snæfellsnes`},{id:`krysuvik-seltun`,name:`Krýsuvík and Seltún`,category:`nature`,tags:[`geothermal`,`mud-pots`,`lake`,`reykjanes`,`free`],area:`Reykjanes Peninsula`,lat:63.8952,lng:-22.05606,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A colourful geothermal field of bubbling mud pots and steam vents at Seltún on a boardwalk loop, reached past the dark lake of Kleifarvatn.`,tip:`About 40 minutes from the city by car; pair it with the Reykjanes coast or the Blue Lagoon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Krýsuvík`},{id:`esja`,name:`Mount Esja Hike`,localName:`Esja`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`mountain`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Mosfellsbær`,lat:64.20926,lng:-21.7124,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The flat-topped mountain across the bay from the city, where a well-marked trail climbs from the Esjustofa car park to the Steinn boulder and on to the summit plateau.`,tip:`Turning back at Steinn, about 2 hours return, gives most of the view; the last scramble to Þverfellshorn is steep.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Esja`}],foods:[{name:`Icelandic hot dog`,localName:`Pylsa`,description:`A lamb-blend sausage in a soft bun with ketchup, sweet mustard, remoulade, raw and crispy fried onions; ask for eina með öllu, one with everything.`},{name:`Icelandic lamb soup`,localName:`Kjötsúpa`,description:`A hearty broth of free-range lamb, root vegetables and herbs, the classic warming bowl on a cold day.`},{name:`Plokkfiskur`,description:`A comforting mash of boiled white fish, potatoes, onion and béchamel, traditionally eaten with buttered rye bread.`},{name:`Langoustine soup`,localName:`Humarsúpa`,description:`A rich, creamy bisque made with Icelandic langoustine, which locals call lobster, a harbour-side favourite.`},{name:`Skyr`,description:`A thick, high-protein cultured dairy product, eaten plain with cream and berries or turned into desserts and cakes.`},{name:`Kleina`,localName:`Kleinur`,description:`Twisted, deep-fried pastry knots flavoured with cardamom, a staple of Icelandic coffee breaks.`}]},{id:`vik`,name:`Vík`,localName:`Vík í Mýrdal`,lat:63.41881,lng:-19.00547,timezone:`Atlantic/Reykjavik`,tagline:`Black-sand beaches, sea stacks and glaciers on the South Coast`,description:`Iceland's southernmost village is a tiny place under green cliffs, but it sits in the middle of the South Coast's greatest hits: waterfalls you can walk behind, black-sand beaches with basalt sea stacks, puffin cliffs and glacier tongues. It makes a natural base for two or three days of driving, with the iceberg lagoon at Jökulsárlón within a long day's reach.`,idealDays:[2,3],places:[{id:`reynisfjara`,name:`Reynisfjara`,category:`nature`,tags:[`beach`,`black-sand`,`basalt`,`iconic`,`sunset`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Reynishverfi`,lat:63.4035,lng:-19.0474,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The famous black-sand beach west of Vík, backed by the hexagonal basalt columns of Gardar and the cave of Hálsanefshellir, with the Reynisdrangar sea stacks rising offshore.`,tip:`Sneaker waves here are deadly: stay at least 30 metres from the water, obey the warning lights at the car park, and never turn your back on the sea.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Reynisfjara`},{id:`vikurfjara`,name:`Vík Beach and Reynisdrangar`,localName:`Víkurfjara`,category:`nature`,tags:[`beach`,`black-sand`,`sea-stacks`,`walking`,`sunset`,`northern-lights`,`free`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.414,lng:-19.008,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The long beach right below the village, with the best straight-on view of the Reynisdrangar sea stacks, said in legend to be trolls caught by the sunrise.`,tip:`On clear winter nights this is the easiest northern lights spot in Vík; walk a few minutes from the street lights towards the shore.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Reynisdrangar`},{id:`vikurkirkja`,name:`Vík Church`,localName:`Víkurkirkja`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`viewpoint`,`photo-spot`,`lupins`,`free`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.42053,lng:-19.00293,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small red-roofed church on the hill above the village, the classic postcard shot of Vík with the sea stacks behind and purple lupins in early summer.`,tip:`Locals say the hill is the safe place to run to if Katla erupts and sends a glacial flood across the plain.`,indoor:!1},{id:`dyrholaey`,name:`Dyrhólaey`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`arch`,`puffins`,`lighthouse`,`cliffs`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Dyrhólaey`,lat:63.39972,lng:-19.12639,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A headland with a huge sea arch, a lighthouse and sweeping views along endless black beaches to the glaciers, with puffins nesting on the cliffs in summer.`,tip:`The upper road needs care and the headland may close for nesting in May and June; puffins are easiest to see from the lower car park on summer evenings.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dyrhólaey`},{id:`skogafoss`,name:`Skógafoss`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`iconic`,`rainbow`,`viewpoint`,`photo-spot`],area:`Skógar`,lat:63.53211,lng:-19.51114,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:5,description:`A thundering 60-metre curtain of water you can walk right up to, with rainbows in the spray on sunny days and a steel staircase climbing to a viewing platform at the top.`,tip:`Pay for parking by app or at the machine. Go early or late in the day; tour buses pack the base from mid-morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Skógafoss`},{id:`kvernufoss`,name:`Kvernufoss`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`hidden-gem`,`walking`,`gorge`,`free`],area:`Skógar`,lat:63.52869,lng:-19.48051,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A quieter waterfall tucked into a mossy gorge just east of Skógar, where a short walk leads you behind the falling water.`,tip:`Park by the Skógar Museum and follow the trail along the fence; it takes about 20 minutes each way.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kvernufoss`},{id:`skogar-museum`,name:`Skógar Museum`,localName:`Skógasafn`,category:`museum`,tags:[`folk-museum`,`turf-houses`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Skógar`,lat:63.52619,lng:-19.49306,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A wonderful jumble of rural life: turf farmhouses and a wooden church outside, fishing boats and old tools inside, plus a museum of transport and communications.`,tip:`Allow time for the outdoor turf houses as well as the main hall; the café in the transport museum is a good lunch stop.`,indoor:!0},{id:`fimmvorduhals-waterfall-way`,name:`Waterfall Way above Skógafoss`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`waterfalls`,`canyon`,`trail`,`free`],area:`Skógar`,lat:63.5295,lng:-19.5125,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The first stretch of the Fimmvörðuháls trail climbs from the top of Skógafoss past more than 20 further waterfalls in a deepening canyon.`,tip:`Walk up as far as you like and return the same way; the full crossing to Þórsmörk is a serious day hike only for summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fimmvörðuháls`},{id:`seljalandsfoss`,name:`Seljalandsfoss`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`iconic`,`walk-behind`,`sunset`,`photo-spot`],area:`Seljaland`,lat:63.61583,lng:-19.99278,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:5,description:`A slender 60-metre waterfall dropping from an old sea cliff, famous for the path that loops right behind the curtain of water.`,tip:`Bring a rain jacket for the path behind the falls, which closes in icy winter conditions; summer evenings light it beautifully.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Seljalandsfoss`},{id:`gljufrabui`,name:`Gljúfrabúi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`hidden-gem`,`canyon`,`free`],area:`Seljaland`,lat:63.62076,lng:-19.98634,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A waterfall hidden inside a narrow cleft in the cliff, a short walk north of Seljalandsfoss; you wade or hop over stones through the gap to see it.`,tip:`Expect wet feet: waterproof boots help, and the stepping stones are slippery.`,indoor:!1},{id:`seljavallalaug`,name:`Seljavallalaug`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`hot-spring`,`swimming`,`historic`,`hiking`],area:`Seljavellir`,lat:63.56614,lng:-19.60756,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`One of Iceland's oldest swimming pools, built in 1923 into a steep green valley under Eyjafjallajökull and fed by a lukewarm natural spring.`,tip:`It is a 20-minute walk from the car park; the water is only tepid and the changing huts are basic, so go for the setting.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Seljavallalaug`},{id:`solheimajokull`,name:`Sólheimajökull Glacier Walk`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`glacier`,`hiking`,`guided-tour`,`ice`,`crampons`],area:`Sólheimajökull`,lat:63.53076,lng:-19.37087,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:105,rating:5,description:`An outlet tongue of Mýrdalsjökull that you can reach on foot from the car park; guided walks with crampons and ice axes lead out among ridges, crevasses and black ash bands.`,tip:`Never walk onto the ice without a guide. Without a tour, the 15-minute path to the glacier edge is free.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sólheimajökull`},{id:`solheimasandur-plane-wreck`,name:`Sólheimasandur Plane Wreck`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`plane-wreck`,`black-sand`,`walking`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Sólheimasandur`,lat:63.45908,lng:-19.36482,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The stripped fuselage of a US Navy plane that crash-landed on the black sand in 1973, now an eerie photo stop at the end of a long, flat walk.`,tip:`It is about 4 km each way from the car park on Route 1; a paid shuttle runs in season, and the walk is grim in wind or rain.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`1973 Sólheimasandur Douglas C-117D crash`},{id:`katla-ice-cave`,name:`Katla Ice Cave Tour`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`ice-cave`,`glacier`,`guided-tour`,`super-jeep`,`year-round`],area:`Mýrdalsjökull (tours from Vík)`,lat:63.4174,lng:-19.0003,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:200,rating:4,description:`Super-jeep tours from Vík drive to the edge of Kötlujökull, where black-streaked ice caves sit beneath the glacier over the Katla volcano.`,tip:`Tours run year-round and leave from Vík; book ahead in summer, and expect the cave to look different each season as the ice moves.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Katla (volcano)`},{id:`hjorleifshofdi`,name:`Hjörleifshöfði`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hill`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`saga`,`black-sand`,`free`],area:`Mýrdalssandur`,lat:63.4167,lng:-18.7667,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lone grassy outcrop rising from the black plains east of Vík, linked to one of the first settlers, with a cave at its base and a loop trail over the top.`,tip:`The gravel track off Route 1 is rough; the cave at the foot is the quick option if you do not want the 1 to 2 hour hike.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hjörleifshöfði`},{id:`fjadrargljufur`,name:`Fjaðrárgljúfur`,category:`nature`,tags:[`canyon`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`moss`,`photo-spot`],area:`Kirkjubæjarklaustur`,lat:63.7713,lng:-18.17187,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:5,description:`A serpentine, 100-metre-deep canyon lined with moss-covered walls, best seen from the platforms along the rim path above the river.`,tip:`Stay on the marked path; the rim closes at times in spring to protect the vegetation.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fjaðrárgljúfur`},{id:`systrafoss`,name:`Kirkjubæjarklaustur and Systrafoss`,category:`culture`,tags:[`waterfall`,`village`,`history`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Kirkjubæjarklaustur`,lat:63.78595,lng:-18.05964,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small village on the site of a medieval convent, with the twin Systrafoss falls tumbling down the cliff behind it and a woodland path to the lake above.`,tip:`Stop nearby at Kirkjugólf, a natural basalt floor once thought to be the foundation of an old church.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Systrafoss`},{id:`dverghamrar`,name:`Dverghamrar`,category:`nature`,tags:[`basalt-columns`,`folklore`,`short-walk`,`free`],area:`Síða`,lat:63.84939,lng:-17.86025,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Dwarf Cliffs, a cluster of neat basalt columns shaped by the sea at the end of the Ice Age, said in folklore to house hidden people.`,tip:`A five-minute stop just off Route 1 east of Kirkjubæjarklaustur; pair it with the Foss á Síðu waterfall nearby.`,indoor:!1},{id:`skaftafell`,name:`Skaftafell and Svartifoss`,category:`nature`,tags:[`national-park`,`hiking`,`waterfall`,`basalt-columns`,`glacier`,`day-trip`],area:`Vatnajökull National Park`,lat:64.01667,lng:-16.96633,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:5,description:`The green oasis of Vatnajökull National Park, where trails lead to Svartifoss, a waterfall framed by black basalt columns, and to the glacier tongue of Skaftafellsjökull.`,tip:`The Svartifoss loop takes about 1.5 hours from the visitor centre; pay the parking fee online and set off early from Vík, about two hours away.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Skaftafell`},{id:`jokulsarlon`,name:`Jökulsárlón and Diamond Beach`,category:`nature`,tags:[`glacier-lagoon`,`icebergs`,`seals`,`boat-tour`,`iconic`,`day-trip`],area:`Breiðamerkursandur`,lat:64.04789,lng:-16.18027,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:5,description:`A glacier lagoon full of blue and white icebergs calved from Breiðamerkurjökull, drifting out to sea and washing up as glittering ice on the black sand of Diamond Beach.`,tip:`A long day from Vík, about 2.5 hours each way: pair it with Fjallsárlón and Skaftafell, and book an amphibian or zodiac boat in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jökulsárlón`},{id:`kotlusetur`,name:`Katla Visitor Centre`,localName:`Kötlusetur`,category:`museum`,tags:[`volcano`,`geopark`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`free`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.41758,lng:-19.01414,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small exhibition in Brydebúð, an 1830s merchant house, on the Katla volcano, its floods and the fishing life of the Vík coast.`,tip:`Combine it with a coffee and cake at Halldórskaffi in the same building.`,indoor:!0},{id:`lava-show-vik`,name:`Icelandic Lava Show`,category:`family`,tags:[`lava`,`show`,`volcano`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.41841,lng:-19.01024,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:57,rating:4,description:`Real molten rock, heated to over 1,100 °C, is poured into a small theatre in front of you while a guide explains Iceland's volcanoes; the original show, opened in Vík in 2018.`,tip:`Book a time slot online; front rows feel the heat, and the show runs in English several times a day.`,indoor:!0},{id:`lava-centre`,name:`Lava Centre`,category:`museum`,tags:[`volcano`,`interactive`,`earthquakes`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Hvolsvöllur`,lat:63.75329,lng:-20.23627,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:38,rating:4,description:`A modern interactive exhibition on Icelandic volcanoes and earthquakes, with a short film and a rooftop view over Eyjafjallajökull and Hekla country.`,tip:`A good rainy-day stop on the drive between Reykjavík and Vík.`,indoor:!0},{id:`icewear-vik`,name:`Icewear Vík Wool Shop`,localName:`Víkurprjón`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`wool`,`sweaters`,`souvenirs`,`outdoor-gear`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.41736,lng:-18.99998,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A big wool and outdoor-clothing store grown from Vík's old knitting factory, good for lopapeysa sweaters, hats and last-minute rain gear.`,tip:`Through the windows at the back you can sometimes see knitting machines at work.`,indoor:!0},{id:`smidjan-brugghus`,name:`Smiðjan Brugghús`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`craft-beer`,`brewery`,`burgers`,`bar`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.41722,lng:-19.01092,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A craft brewery and bar in an old workshop in the village, the liveliest place in Vík for an evening beer after a day on the South Coast.`,tip:`Try a tasting flight of the house beers; it gets busy at dinner time in summer.`,indoor:!0},{id:`vik-swimming-pool`,name:`Vík Swimming Pool`,localName:`Sundlaugin í Vík`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`hot-tub`,`local-life`,`geothermal`],area:`Vík village`,lat:63.41689,lng:-19.00784,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`The village's small heated outdoor pool and hot tubs, a cheap and very local way to warm up after a cold day of sightseeing.`,tip:`As at every Icelandic pool, shower without a swimsuit before you get in; check opening hours, which are shorter in winter.`,indoor:!1}],foods:[{name:`Icelandic lamb soup`,localName:`Kjötsúpa`,description:`A hearty broth of free-range lamb, root vegetables and herbs, the classic warming bowl on a cold South Coast day.`},{name:`Arctic char`,localName:`Bleikja`,description:`A delicate, pink-fleshed cousin of salmon and trout, often farmed in clean spring water in the south and served pan-fried.`},{name:`Plokkfiskur`,description:`A comforting mash of boiled white fish, potatoes, onion and béchamel, traditionally eaten with buttered rye bread.`},{name:`Icelandic hot dog`,localName:`Pylsa`,description:`A lamb-blend sausage in a soft bun with ketchup, sweet mustard, remoulade, raw and crispy fried onions, sold at every fuel station.`},{name:`Skyr`,description:`A thick, high-protein cultured dairy product, eaten plain with cream and berries or turned into desserts and cakes.`}]},{id:`akureyri`,name:`Akureyri`,lat:65.68262,lng:-18.09064,timezone:`Atlantic/Reykjavik`,tagline:`Fjord-side town, Mývatn lava fields and Húsavík whales`,description:`Iceland's second town sits at the head of the long Eyjafjörður fjord, a friendly place of colourful wooden houses, a hilltop church, a famous botanic garden and a lively café and music scene. It is the gateway to the volcanic wonders of Lake Mývatn, the waterfalls Goðafoss and Dettifoss, and whale watching from Húsavík.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`akureyrarkirkja`,name:`Akureyri Church`,localName:`Akureyrarkirkja`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`,`free`],area:`Miðbær`,lat:65.6799,lng:-18.0908,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The twin-towered 1940 church by Guðjón Samúelsson, designer of Hallgrímskirkja, reached by a long flight of steps from the town centre with views over the fjord.`,tip:`Look for the stained-glass window that came from Coventry Cathedral in England; the church is often closed outside services in winter.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Akureyrarkirkja`},{id:`botanical-garden`,name:`Akureyri Botanical Garden`,localName:`Lystigarðurinn`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`flowers`,`cafe`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Suðurbrekka`,lat:65.67511,lng:-18.09367,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of the world's most northerly botanic gardens, with thousands of Icelandic and imported plants flowering surprisingly well in the mild fjord climate.`,tip:`At its best from June to August; the glass-walled café Laufið in the garden is a lovely coffee stop.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Akureyri Botanical Garden`},{id:`hafnarstraeti`,name:`Hafnarstræti and Town Centre`,localName:`Hafnarstræti`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`pedestrian-street`,`shops`,`cafes`,`heart-traffic-lights`,`walking`],area:`Miðbær`,lat:65.6815,lng:-18.0893,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The short pedestrian heart of Akureyri, lined with design and wool shops, bookshops, bakeries and bars around the Ráðhústorg square.`,tip:`Notice the heart-shaped red traffic lights, a small cheer-up gesture the town added after the 2008 financial crash.`,indoor:!1},{id:`akureyri-art-museum`,name:`Akureyri Art Museum`,localName:`Listasafnið á Akureyri`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`gallery`,`rainy-day`],area:`Listagil`,lat:65.68044,lng:-18.092,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A bright contemporary art museum in a converted dairy on Listagil, the arts street, showing Icelandic and international exhibitions.`,tip:`Climb to the rooftop terrace for a view over the town and fjord.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Akureyri Art Museum`},{id:`akureyri-museum`,name:`Akureyri Museum`,localName:`Minjasafnið á Akureyri`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`local-life`,`old-town`,`rainy-day`],area:`Innbærinn`,lat:65.66689,lng:-18.08522,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`The town and regional history museum in the old quarter, covering settlement, farming and town life, with a pretty garden and a small wooden church.`,tip:`The ticket usually also covers Nonni's House next door, so do both together.`,indoor:!0},{id:`nonnahus`,name:`Nonni's House`,localName:`Nonnahús`,category:`museum`,tags:[`historic-house`,`literature`,`old-town`,`rainy-day`],area:`Innbærinn`,lat:65.66706,lng:-18.08576,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`The tiny 1850 timber childhood home of Jón Sveinsson, the Jesuit priest whose Nonni children's books were translated into dozens of languages.`,tip:`Walk back to town along Aðalstræti, the street of the oldest houses in Akureyri.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Nonni's House`},{id:`hof`,name:`Hof Cultural Centre`,localName:`Menningarhúsið Hof`,category:`culture`,tags:[`concerts`,`theatre`,`architecture`,`waterfront`,`rainy-day`],area:`Waterfront`,lat:65.68336,lng:-18.08741,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:3,description:`The round, basalt-clad concert and conference hall on the harbour, home to the North Iceland Symphony Orchestra and touring shows.`,tip:`The tourist information desk and a bistro are on the ground floor, open even when nothing is on stage.`,indoor:!0},{id:`graeni-hatturinn`,name:`Græni hatturinn`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`live-music`,`bar`,`concerts`,`local-life`],area:`Miðbær`,lat:65.68138,lng:-18.08946,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`The Green Hat, a cosy basement venue on Hafnarstræti that is one of Iceland's best-loved small stages for Icelandic bands, folk and rock.`,tip:`Gigs are mostly Thursday to Saturday and the best shows sell out; buy tickets online in advance.`,indoor:!0},{id:`akureyri-swimming-pool`,name:`Akureyri Swimming Pool`,localName:`Sundlaug Akureyrar`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`hot-tub`,`waterslides`,`geothermal`,`local-life`,`kids`],area:`Brekkan`,lat:65.67911,lng:-18.09821,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`One of Iceland's favourite town pools, with outdoor lap pools, hot tubs, a steam room and big water slides, open late into the evening.`,tip:`Shower without a swimsuit before you swim, as at every Icelandic pool; locals gather in the hot tubs after work.`,indoor:!1},{id:`forest-lagoon`,name:`Forest Lagoon`,localName:`Skógarböðin`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`spa`,`lagoon`,`forest`,`northern-lights`,`sunset`],area:`Vaðlaskógur`,lat:65.66992,lng:-18.0418,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`A geothermal lagoon set among birch and pine trees on the slope across the fjord from Akureyri, with infinity-edge views of the town and a swim-up bar.`,tip:`Book a time slot online; evenings in winter can bring northern lights over the fjord while you soak.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kjarnaskogur`,name:`Kjarnaskógur Forest`,localName:`Kjarnaskógur`,category:`family`,tags:[`forest`,`walking`,`playground`,`picnic`,`free`],area:`South Akureyri`,lat:65.64716,lng:-18.08448,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A planted forest on the southern edge of town, rare in Iceland, with walking and biking trails, playgrounds and barbecue spots.`,tip:`In winter the trails are groomed for cross-country skiing and lit after dark.`,indoor:!1},{id:`hlidarfjall`,name:`Hlíðarfjall`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`skiing`,`hiking`,`mountain`,`viewpoint`,`winter`],area:`Hlíðarfjall`,lat:65.6487,lng:-18.2659,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:3,description:`Iceland's leading ski area, a few minutes' drive above town, with lifts and long runs from roughly December to April and hiking trails in summer.`,tip:`Hiking in summer is free; ski days are best in March and April when the days are longer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hlíðarfjall`},{id:`christmas-garden`,name:`Christmas Garden`,localName:`Jólagarðurinn`,category:`family`,tags:[`christmas`,`shop`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`free`],area:`Eyjafjarðarsveit`,lat:65.58011,lng:-18.0915,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A year-round Christmas house in a red gingerbread-style cottage south of town, packed with decorations, sweets and the stories of Iceland's 13 Yule Lads.`,tip:`Free to enter; a quick stop on the drive south along the fjord.`,indoor:!0},{id:`laufas`,name:`Laufás Turf Farm`,localName:`Laufás`,category:`culture`,tags:[`turf-houses`,`history`,`church`,`museum`],area:`Eyjafjörður east shore`,lat:65.89374,lng:-18.07184,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`A beautifully kept 19th-century turf-roofed parsonage beside a small church, furnished as it was when a pastor's household of 20 or more lived here.`,tip:`Open mainly in summer; it is about 30 minutes from Akureyri on the way to Húsavík.`,indoor:!0},{id:`hrisey`,name:`Hrísey Island`,localName:`Hrísey`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`ferry`,`birdwatching`,`walking`,`village`],area:`Eyjafjörður`,lat:66.00336,lng:-18.38474,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`The Pearl of Eyjafjörður, a quiet, almost car-free island reached by a 15-minute ferry, with a small fishing village, nesting birds and easy walking loops.`,tip:`Drive 35 minutes north to Árskógssandur for the ferry; watch out for nesting Arctic terns in early summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hrísey`},{id:`beer-spa`,name:`Beer Spa`,localName:`Bjórböðin`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`spa`,`beer`,`hot-tubs`,`brewery`,`unusual`],area:`Árskógssandur`,lat:65.94502,lng:-18.36258,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:100,rating:3,description:`A quirky spa next to the Kaldi brewery where you soak in wooden tubs of young beer, water, hops and yeast, with a tap beside you, then sit in outdoor hot tubs.`,tip:`Book ahead; it pairs well with the Hrísey ferry, which leaves from the same village.`,indoor:!0},{id:`herring-era-museum`,name:`Herring Era Museum`,localName:`Síldarminjasafn Íslands`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`fishing`,`maritime`,`rainy-day`,`day-trip`],area:`Siglufjörður`,lat:66.1485,lng:-18.913,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:33,rating:4,description:`Iceland's largest maritime museum, telling the boom-town story of the herring years in three buildings, including a salting station and a harbour of old boats.`,tip:`The drive via the Tröllaskagi tunnels and Ólafsfjörður is scenic; in summer there are sometimes herring-salting shows.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Herring Era Museum`},{id:`godafoss`,name:`Goðafoss`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`iconic`,`history`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Bárðardalur`,lat:65.68282,lng:-17.55062,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The Waterfall of the Gods, a wide horseshoe of falls where, legend says, the lawspeaker threw his pagan idols after Iceland adopted Christianity in 1000.`,tip:`Walk both banks: the east side gives the classic view, and a path on the west side goes down to the river.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Goðafoss`},{id:`skutustadagigar`,name:`Skútustaðir Pseudocraters`,localName:`Skútustaðagígar`,category:`nature`,tags:[`craters`,`lake`,`birdwatching`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Mývatn`,lat:65.5709,lng:-17.0349,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A cluster of grassy pseudocraters on the south shore of Lake Mývatn, formed when lava flowed over wetlands and steam blasted through it.`,tip:`Midges can be fierce on still summer days; a head net costs little and helps a lot.`,indoor:!1},{id:`dimmuborgir`,name:`Dimmuborgir`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lava-formations`,`hiking`,`folklore`,`yule-lads`],area:`Mývatn`,lat:65.58661,lng:-16.89534,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The Dark Castles, a maze of towering lava pillars and arches left by a collapsed lava lake, with marked trails from short loops to longer walks.`,tip:`In folklore this is home to the Yule Lads; the Church loop is the classic route to the cave-like Kirkjan arch.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dimmuborgir`},{id:`hverfjall`,name:`Hverfjall`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`crater`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`volcano`,`free`],area:`Mývatn`,lat:65.60506,lng:-16.87395,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A huge, perfectly round tephra crater about 1 km across, with a steep path to the rim and a walk around it for views over the whole Mývatn area.`,tip:`The rim walk takes about an hour; it is very exposed, so skip it in strong wind.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hverfjall`},{id:`grjotagja`,name:`Grjótagjá`,category:`nature`,tags:[`cave`,`hot-spring`,`game-of-thrones`,`fissure`,`free`],area:`Mývatn`,lat:65.63022,lng:-16.87954,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A small lava cave in a fissure between the tectonic plates, with a pool of crystal-blue geothermal water inside, made famous by Game of Thrones.`,tip:`Bathing is not allowed now as the water is too hot and the cave is on private land; look, do not touch.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Grjótagjá`},{id:`hverir`,name:`Hverir`,category:`nature`,tags:[`geothermal`,`mud-pots`,`fumaroles`,`iconic`,`photo-spot`],area:`Námafjall`,lat:65.64114,lng:-16.80918,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`An otherworldly field of boiling mud pots and roaring steam vents in orange and ochre ground at the foot of Námafjall, smelling strongly of sulphur.`,tip:`Stay on the roped paths, as the crust can be thin and scalding; climb Námafjall ridge behind for a broader view.`,indoor:!1},{id:`myvatn-nature-baths`,name:`Mývatn Nature Baths`,localName:`Jarðböðin við Mývatn`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`lagoon`,`spa`,`northern-lights`,`sunset`],area:`Mývatn`,lat:65.6304,lng:-16.8476,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:4,description:`The milky-blue geothermal lagoon of the north, quieter than the Blue Lagoon, with views over lava fields and steaming hills that are magical on winter evenings.`,tip:`The baths are being rebuilt as the larger Earth Lagoon Mývatn, so check the current name, prices and opening hours before you go.`,indoor:!1},{id:`krafla-viti`,name:`Krafla and Víti Crater`,category:`nature`,tags:[`volcano`,`crater-lake`,`lava-field`,`geothermal`,`hiking`],area:`Krafla`,lat:65.7171,lng:-16.7531,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An active volcanic area where you can walk the rim of Víti, a milky-green crater lake, and cross the still-steaming Leirhnjúkur lava fields of the 1980s eruptions.`,tip:`The road up passes the geothermal power station; the Leirhnjúkur loop takes about an hour on marked paths.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Krafla`},{id:`husavik-whale-watching`,name:`Húsavík Whale Watching`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`whales`,`boat-tour`,`puffins`,`wildlife`,`iconic`],area:`Húsavík`,lat:66.04629,lng:-17.34372,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`Iceland's whale-watching capital, where oak boats and RIBs head into Skjálfandi Bay for humpbacks, minke whales, dolphins and sometimes blue whales in summer.`,tip:`Sightings are best from June to August; take seasickness tablets and wear the warm overalls the operators lend.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Húsavík`},{id:`husavik-whale-museum`,name:`Húsavík Whale Museum`,localName:`Hvalasafnið á Húsavík`,category:`museum`,tags:[`whales`,`skeletons`,`wildlife`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Húsavík`,lat:66.04692,lng:-17.3441,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:24,rating:4,description:`A museum in an old slaughterhouse by the harbour, with hanging whale skeletons, including a blue whale, and exhibits on whale biology and conservation.`,tip:`Visit after your boat trip to put names to the whales you saw.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Húsavík Whale Museum`},{id:`geosea`,name:`GeoSea Geothermal Sea Baths`,localName:`Sjóböðin`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`geothermal`,`sea-view`,`spa`,`sunset`,`northern-lights`],area:`Húsavík`,lat:66.05262,lng:-17.36129,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:65,rating:4,description:`Infinity pools of warm geothermal seawater on a headland above Húsavík, looking straight out over Skjálfandi Bay to the mountains, and sometimes to spouting whales.`,tip:`Perfect after whale watching; in June the midnight sun hangs over the bay late into the night.`,indoor:!1},{id:`dettifoss`,name:`Dettifoss and Ásbyrgi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`canyon`,`national-park`,`iconic`,`day-trip`],area:`Vatnajökull National Park (Jökulsárgljúfur)`,lat:65.81435,lng:-16.38449,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Europe's most powerful waterfall, a roaring grey wall of glacial meltwater in the Jökulsá canyon, combined with the horseshoe cliffs of Ásbyrgi on a long Diamond Circle day.`,tip:`Route 862 on the west side is paved and open longer; the east road is gravel and closes in winter. Visit Selfoss a short walk upstream.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dettifoss`}],foods:[{name:`Icelandic lamb`,localName:`Lambakjöt`,description:`Free-roaming lamb raised on mountain grass and herbs, served as roast leg, chops or slow-cooked shank with potatoes.`},{name:`Rúgbrauð with smoked trout`,localName:`Hverabrauð`,description:`Dark, sweet rye bread slow-baked in hot geothermal ground around Mývatn, eaten with butter and local smoked trout or char.`},{name:`Plokkfiskur`,description:`A comforting mash of boiled white fish, potatoes, onion and béchamel, traditionally eaten with buttered rye bread.`},{name:`Brynja ice cream`,localName:`Brynjuís`,description:`Akureyri's cult soft-serve, made with a local recipe since the 1940s and dipped in chocolate or blended with sweets.`},{name:`Icelandic hot dog`,localName:`Pylsa`,description:`A lamb-blend sausage in a soft bun with ketchup, sweet mustard, remoulade, raw and crispy fried onions.`},{name:`Skyr`,description:`A thick, high-protein cultured dairy product, eaten plain with cream and berries or turned into desserts and cakes.`}]}]};export{e as iceland};